    "explanation": "The rider filed this dispute, so the outcome is read from the rider's claim against the record. The 4.00 SGD no-show cancellation fee charged at 17:33:14 is voided and returned to the rider.\n\nWhat is not in dispute. The driver was at the pickup: his 17:26:45 arrival marker is corroborated by the driver-device trace, whose nearest fix sits 2.7 m from the pickup point at 6 m reported accuracy — inside the 50 m STANDARD-zone arrival radius and inside the 25 m accuracy filter (POL-NS-21). This on-demand trip carries no scheduled time, so the 300 s free wait ran from arrival at 17:26:45 and expired at 17:31:45; the driver cancelled at 17:33:10, 85 s later, so the free wait was served and he was entitled to treat the rider as a no-show. On the driver's POL-NS-24 point: that clause gives the rider nothing here — the driver arrived, and he did make contact attempts, so the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit is not engaged.\n\nThe fee nonetheless does not stand. POL-NS-23 requires the driver, before cancelling for no-show, to have sent at least one in-app chat message AND placed at least one in-app call to the rider. The messaging limb is met: two messages at 17:27:00 and 17:30:10, both delivered and read before cancellation. The call limb is met nowhere: trip_record.in_app_calls is empty (call_count 0, no entries) and the chat log holds only the two text messages, with no voice-call entry. The driver's own statement — 'I messaged 2 times, waited 6 minutes' — asserts messaging and waiting only, matching the record, so the one party with every reason to mention a call confirms none was made. POL-NS-23 provides that if either limb is missing the fee is voided and the rider is not charged, with no driver compensation. The driver's argument that the missing call is a mere 'formality' that cannot enlarge what is in issue is rejected: POL-NS-23 makes the call a condition of charging, and a served free wait under POL-NS-21 speaks only to when the driver MAY cancel — it cannot cure the separate contact condition POL-NS-23 imposes. The money figures are read off the fare breakdown: cancellation_fee 4.00 SGD, total_charged 4.00 SGD, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The whole contested amount, 4.00 SGD, is returned: FULL_REFUND, with no driver compensation.\n\nThe driver's point that the present state stands unless the claim is made out is answered: the claim is made out, on POL-NS-23. The missing traffic advisory (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and is not needed here: the deciding facts sit on the trip record and the chat log, both COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged and no fact needed by any rule is unavailable. The dispute value is 4.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither profile carries a fraud flag, so this AI ruling is final at any confidence (POL-GEN-22, POL-NS-26). The repeat no-show flag in POL-NS-25 is not engaged: the profile field it names is absent, and the fee does not stand so this trip does not count toward it.\n\nThe referral below adds to the money ruling and does not displace it (POL-GEN-03).",
